activity-receipt-operation = Reported App: { $app } · Operation: { $operation }
activity-receipt-package-digest = Reported App package digest
activity-receipt-result-json = JSON
activity-receipt-result-text = Text
activity-receipt-result-empty = Empty
activity-receipt-result-summary = Reported result: { $kind } · Reported bytes: { $bytes }
activity-receipt-result-digest = Reported original-output SHA-256
activity-receipt-digest-caveat = A digest of output as reported by the caller, not a cryptographic OS execution attestation.
activity-receipt-preview-hint = Bounded, possibly redacted preview. Displayed as inert plain text, not trusted markup or commands.
activity-receipt-truncated = This preview is truncated.
activity-receipt-no-result = No result summary was reported.
activity-receipt-error = Caller-reported error
activity-receipt-declaration = Historical App declaration snapshot
activity-receipt-declaration-caveat = Metadata authenticated at recording time only, not current App validity or proof of reported execution, outcome, or effects. The report remains CALLER-REPORTED. Recovery is historical App-declared guidance, never a guarantee.
activity-receipt-declaration-unavailable = No authenticated declaration snapshot was recorded. The caller report is retained.
activity-receipt-no-declared-effects = No App effect declarations were recorded; actual effects remain unknown.
activity-receipt-indeterminate-hint = Indeterminate means the reported outcome is uncertain, not success or proof that no effects occurred.

activity-object-state = Object state
activity-object-state-caveat = Classifications are caller reports, not verified facts. Statements, inferences and planning relations grant no authority, run no App or model, and never complete the goal.
activity-object-state-window-caveat = Time windows are reported validity only. Being within a reported window does not make an observation true, current, verified or fresh.
activity-object-state-snapshot-hint = Window status is the broker's projection at the last object-state refresh. Refresh again to update it.
activity-object-state-refresh = Refresh object state
activity-object-state-new = Add observation / relation
activity-object-state-filter = Exact App reference filter (optional)
activity-object-state-filter-hint = Use an exact canonical reference from resources or history, including detached references. Clear this field to list all subjects, then refresh.
activity-object-state-load-hint = Refresh to read shared annotation history. This does not fetch or execute an App.
activity-object-state-empty = No entries were returned for this filter. No object state is inferred.
activity-object-state-limit = At most 100 entries are shown from the shared ledger, which holds at most 1000 per Activity. Filter by reference to narrow history; no local history store is created.
activity-object-state-no-resources = Attach a canonical App object reference to author an observation. Existing history remains readable even without attached resources.
activity-object-state-subject = Subject App reference
activity-object-state-target = Target App reference
activity-object-state-resource-required = Select subject and relation target references already attached to this Activity. The broker validates their canonical form.
activity-object-state-user-statement = User statement (caller classification)
activity-object-state-agent-inference = Agent inference (caller classification)
activity-object-state-app-report = App receipt link (caller classification)
activity-object-state-relation = Planning relation (caller classification)
activity-object-state-retracted = Retracted entry; history retained
activity-object-state-related-to = Related to (planning only)
activity-object-state-depends-on = Depends on (planning only)
activity-object-state-derived-from = Derived from (planning only)
activity-object-state-text = Reported statement / inference (nonempty, at most 4096 UTF-8 bytes)
activity-object-state-note = Relation note (optional, at most 2048 UTF-8 bytes)
activity-object-state-reason = Retraction reason (nonempty, at most 4096 UTF-8 bytes)
activity-object-state-receipt-id = Existing Activity receipt ID
activity-object-state-receipt-required = Enter a valid UUID for an existing Activity receipt.
activity-object-state-app-caveat = An App-linked receipt is still caller_reported, not proof that its result concerns this object. The broker requires an existing same-owner, same-Activity, same-App receipt. No replacement App text is accepted.
activity-object-state-observed-at = Reported window start (RFC3339)
activity-object-state-valid-until = Reported window end (RFC3339)
activity-object-state-window-hint = Leave both fields empty, or supply RFC3339 timestamps with end after start (for example 2026-09-11T12:00:00Z). The broker validates the window. Relations and retractions have no time window.
activity-object-state-unknown = No reported window; validity unknown
activity-object-state-not-yet-applicable = Reported window has not started
activity-object-state-within-window = Within reported window; not verified freshness
activity-object-state-expired = Reported window expired
activity-object-state-entry-id = Entry ID
activity-object-state-draft-id = Submission UUID
activity-object-state-recorded-hint = Broker recording time, not confirmation of observation time or object freshness.
activity-object-state-no-successor = No recorded successor in this response; not a truth or freshness claim.
activity-object-state-superseded = Superseded by { $id }; this historical entry is retained.
activity-object-state-supersedes = Supersedes entry
activity-object-state-detached = This subject reference is detached. History remains readable; reattach the exact canonical reference before appending a correction or retraction.
activity-object-state-correct = Correct with a new entry
activity-object-state-retract = Retract with a reason
activity-object-state-correction-hint = The subject is fixed. This appends a new immutable entry with one predecessor; only one successor is allowed. Stale corrections conflict. Discard and refresh before correcting a newer entry. Retractions cannot be corrected; add a fresh observation instead.
activity-object-state-correction-unavailable = This entry is superseded, retracted, detached or no longer selected. Refresh the history before correcting or retracting it.
activity-object-state-retry-hint = Retrying an unchanged submission reuses this UUID. Editing after a submission creates a new UUID. A timeout may have recorded the entry; retry unchanged before editing to avoid an unintended extra entry.
activity-object-state-save = Record caller report
activity-object-state-discard = Discard draft / refresh history
activity-object-state-recorded = Recorded caller report { $id }. Activity lifecycle is unchanged.
